meta {
  name: 04 System prompt override - Ollama gemma4
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{aiUwLambdaUrl}}/workflows/field-extraction/run
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "url": "https://rbi-files.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/loan_applications/634/documents/cogs-1761837988349-COGS.pdf",
    "fields": {
      "entity_legal_name": {
        "label": "entity legal name",
        "type": "string",
        "required": true
      },
      "issuing_state": {
        "label": "issuing state",
        "type": "string",
        "required": true
      },
      "issue_date": {
        "label": "issue date",
        "type": "date",
        "required": true
      },
      "good_through_valid_until_date": {
        "label": "good-through / valid-until date",
        "type": "date",
        "required": true
      },
      "state_file_number": {
        "label": "state file number",
        "type": "string",
        "required": true
      },
      "status_language": {
        "label": "status language",
        "type": "string",
        "required": true
      },
      "authorized_signature_or_seal_of_the_secretary_of_state": {
        "label": "authorized signature or seal of the Secretary of State",
        "type": "string",
        "required": true
      }
    },
    "expected_class": "certificateOfGoodStanding",
    "model": "gemma4:31b-cloud",
    "max_pages": 10,
    "system_prompt": "You are the document extraction layer for RBI Private Lending's AI underwriting engine (TEST OVERRIDE). Read ONE uploaded document and return structured facts only, as the JSON envelope described in the user message. Never infer a value that is not legibly present: return null and say why in unreadable_fields. Give every field its own confidence between 0 and 1. Dates are ISO 8601. Names verbatim as printed.",
    "instructions": "The entity name must be returned exactly as printed including punctuation and suffix. Return both the issue date and any separate 'good through' date — they are often different. Extract the status language verbatim rather than summarizing it, since 'active', 'in good standing', 'delinquent', and 'administratively dissolved' are all materially different."
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  `system_prompt` replaces the built-in SYSTEM_PROMPT when non-blank (Django
  stores the global prompt, versioned; its seed is byte-identical to the
  built-in one, so Django will normally send the full text). A blank or
  whitespace-only value falls back to the default.

  This request sends a short test prompt to show the override reaches the
  model. The envelope shape is enforced by the user prompt + normalization, not
  by the system prompt, so the response shape is the same as 00.

  Route: Bruno → dispatcher Function URL → ai-uw-utils (`field-extraction`,
  shared/extraction.py run_field_extraction). This is the call Django makes in
  POS Step 1.5, after a document passes step-1 content review.

  Provider is picked by `model`: an id with a ":" (gemma4:31b-cloud,
  gpt-oss:120b-cloud) runs on Ollama Cloud; anything else (gpt-5.2) on OpenAI.
  `ft:` fine-tune ids stay on OpenAI.

  Input contract:
    url, fields {name: {label, type, required}}, expected_class, model,
    max_pages, system_prompt? (replaces the default when non-blank),
    instructions? (ruleset class_specific_instructions), context? (unused by Django)
  Fields and instructions here are copied from ruleset v1.1.0
  (rbi-extraction-prompts.json).

  Response: the extraction envelope — status ok|error, document_class(+confidence),
  class_matches_expected, page_count_received, pages_read, strategy
  (text|vision|image|spreadsheet), model (who actually answered), fields
  {name: {value, confidence, page, verbatim}}, unreadable_fields, signatures,
  integrity_signals, error. Every requested field is always present; an unread
  one is null at confidence 0. Failures come back as status=error with the same
  keys, never as a bare exception.

  Timing: Ollama cold starts can take minutes. The whole run is bounded by
  FIELD_EXTRACTION_BUDGET_SECONDS=780 on utils; the request timeout is off
  (timeout: 0) so Bruno waits it out. Needs ai-underwriting-workflows PR #70 deployed (it raises
  the dispatcher and utils timeouts from 300s to 900s — before that, a long
  Ollama run is cut off at 300s).
}
